course: dictionary
lesson: 15531
title: Suckle: how baby mammals feed
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To suckle means to feed a baby with milk from your body, or, for a baby, to drink milk from its mother. Mammals suckle their young, so a mother cat suckles her kittens and a mother cow suckles her calf.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The lamb ran to its mother and began to suckle.» The lamb is hungry and it runs to its mother, so suckle must mean drinking milk from her.
explain: Suckle is the action, and suckling is the word for it while it is happening. «The piglets were suckling when the farmer arrived» means they were drinking their mother's milk at that moment.
fact: To suckle means to feed a baby with milk from its mother's body.
fact: All mammals suckle their young, including cows, cats, whales, kangaroos and humans.
fact: A kangaroo joey suckles inside its mother's pouch until it is big enough to come out.
fact: «A suckling pig» is a young pig that still drinks its mother's milk.
fact: Suckle is a verb: suckles, suckled and suckling are its other forms.
exercise: «The lamb ran to its mother and began to suckle.» What does suckle mean here? | *Drink milk from its mother | Run fast across the field | Sleep under a tree | Bleat loudly for help
exercise: Which of these animals will suckle its young? | A hen that lays eggs in a nest | A fish that lays eggs in the sea | A snake that lays eggs under a log | *A cow that feeds her calf with milk
exercise: «The piglet was still suckling from its mother.» What is a «suckling pig»? | A pig that lives in a sty | A pig with a curly tail | *A young pig that still drinks its mother's milk | A pig that can swim very fast
test: «The mother cat suckles her kittens every day.» Who is feeding the milk? | The kittens | *The mother cat | The farmer | The dog next door
test: Which group of animals do all suckle their young? | Insects | Birds | *Mammals | Fish
exam: «Whales are mammals, so the mother whale suckles her calf.» What does suckles mean? | *Feeds her baby with milk from her body | Swims away from danger | Sings a song to her calf | Hunts for food in the deep sea
